WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.800
Here's Oracle's starting point.

2
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:06.086
Oracle's CLI reference documents
the announcements list command,

3
00:00:06.086 --> 00:00:09.670
with a required compartment,
an option to read all pages,

4
00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:13.800
and an option to show only the
latest announcement in each chain.

5
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.986
Oracle's Announcement model gives
the fields: the type, two generic

6
00:00:17.986 --> 00:00:22.400
time fields each with its own type,
the lifecycle state and the chain ID.

7
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.028
A separate get command returns
one announcement's details,

8
00:00:26.028 --> 00:00:28.175
including its affected resources.

9
00:00:28.175 --> 00:00:32.280
Oracle's policy reference makes
announcements a resource type:

10
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.300
inspect lists summaries,
read adds the details.

11
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.192
And Oracle's common policy
is a single statement

12
00:00:38.192 --> 00:00:41.350
that lets a group read
announcements in the tenancy.
